  "description": "The 2026 Alabama gubernatorial election will be held on November 3, 2026, to elect the governor of Alabama. Republican incumbent Kay Ivey is term-limited and cannot seek a third term, creating an open seat. The general election features a rematch of the 2020 U.S. Senate race: Republican U.S. Senator Tommy Tuberville faces Democratic former U.S. Senator Doug Jones. Alabama has not elected a Democratic governor since 1998, making this a heavily Republican-leaning race, though Jones's 2017 special election victory demonstrates Democratic competitiveness under specific circumstances.",
